l\nFor Institutes and Chairs\nOffice Hours\nSubmenu: Office Hours\nInternship Office\nStudy Counseling\nStudy Abroad Counseling\nMentoring\nPsychological Counseling\nDean's Office\nDoctoral Studies\nNews\nSubmenu: News\nEvents\nNews\nResearch\nSubmenu: Research\nInstitutions\nSubmenu: Institutions\nInstitutes and Chairs of the Faculty\nAffiliated-Institutes\nExcellence Cluster\nFraunhofer Institutes\nGraduate Research Training Groups\nGraduate School\nProject Houses\nCollaborative Research Centers and Transregio SFBs\nOther Programs\nResearch Associations and Groups\nSubmenu: Research Associations and Groups\nDFG - Research Units\nDWI \u2013 Leibniz Institute for Interactive Materials\nI\u00b3 - Interdisciplinary Integrated Institutes\nJARA\nInterdisciplinary Research Partnerships\nPriority Programs\nTransfer\nSubmenu: Transfer\nSponsoring and Fundraising\nSubmenu: Sponsoring and Fundraising\nSponsoring and Fundraising\nRecruiting\nSubmenu: Recruiting\nStarting out on Career\nFaculty 4\nSubmenu: Faculty 4\nProfile\nSubmenu: Profile\nAbout us\nHistory\nSustainability\nGender Equality\nDean's Office\nSubmenu: Dean's Office\nDean and Vice Deans\nAssistants to the Dean and Employees\nProfessors\nSubmenu: Professors\nProfessorships\nAssistant Professors\nAssociate Professors\nLecturers\napl Professors\nHonorary Professors\nBoards and Committees\nSubmenu: Boards and Committees\nStudy Advisory Council\nStudent Learning Assessment Committee\nBudget Committee\nFaculty Council\nStructural Committee\nExamination Board\nCommission for Equal Opportunities\nQuality Improvement Funds\n*** Gruppenvertretung der Besch\u00e4ftigten in Technik und Verwaltung (BTV) ***\nFor Chairs and Institutes\nSubmenu: For Chairs and Institutes\napl/Honorary Professorship\nPostdoctoral Lecture Qualification\nHonorary Doctorate\nCareer\nSubmenu: Career\nJobs\nContact\nSubmenu: Contact\nContact\nMap\nNews\nSubmenu: News\nCommittee meeting dates\nNews\nEvents\nEvents\nFaculties\nSubmenu: Faculties\nFaculty 1\nMathematics and Natural Sciences\nFaculty 2\nArchitecture\nFaculty 3\nCivil Engineering\nFaculty 4\nMechanical Engineering\nFaculty 5\nGeoresources and Materials Engineering\nFaculty 6\nElectrical Engineering and Information Technology\nFaculty 7\nArts and Humanities\nFaculty 8\nBusiness and Economics\nFaculty 9\nComputer Science\nFaculty 10\nMedicine\nQuick Access\nTools\nRWTHonline\nRWTHcontacts\nRWTHmoodle\nIntranet\nServices\nDining Hall Menus\nRWTH Navigator\nStudent Resources and Support\nOfficial Announcements\nInstitutions\nUniversity Library\nIT Center\nCenter for Teaching and Learning Services\nAthletics and Recreation\nCentral University Administration\nSearch by Name\nSearch for\nSearch\nFaculty of Mechanical Engineering\nYou Are Here:\nStart\nAcademics\nGraduates\nDoctoral Studies\nDuring Your Doctoral Studies\nDoctoral Studies Process\nDoctoral Studies Process\nPlease note that this outlines the typical course of doctoral studies!\nStart Phase \u2013 about two years:\nSince you generally conduct your doctoral studies at the Faculty of Mechanical Engineering within the framework of the a \"Assistenzpromotion,\" the doctoral process begins with signing an empoyment contract and being hired at one of the Faculty's chairs. If the head of the chair showed their willingness to act as the scientific supervisor of your doctoral process, you can also enroll in the RWTH Doctoral Academy. You can find more information on this here.\nWithin the first two years of the doctoral process you must submit an application for assessment of eligiblity for admission to the Faculty's Office for Doctoral Studies. T o do so you must submit a supervision agreement signed by you and your supervisor and, if necessary, recommendations for additional requirement courses. The Dean's Office reviews the prerequisites and the possible additional requirement courses and your application is then approved by the Faculty Council/Council of Elders.\nPlease note that the application must be received by the Faculty's Office for Doctoral Studies no later than three weeks before the respective Faculty Council Meeting/Council of Elders Meeting. The receipt stamp is considered the date of submission. You can find the dates of their meetings here.\nAs soon as your application for assessment of eligibility for admission has been accepted, you can enroll as a doctoral candidate in the Registrar's Office. However this is not required to complee your doctoral studies at RWTH:\nMain Phase \u2013 about three years:\nWhile you are working on your docotrate, your supervisor will regularly advise you. If you still have to complete additional requirements for admission, you will be notified by the Faculty. You have three semesters to complete the additional requirements.\nAs soon as the additional requirements have been fulfilled and you have completed your dissertation, you must submit an application for admission to the doctoral examination. You can find the necessary forms and attachments here. The Faculty Council/Council of Elders is responsible for deciding if you can be admitted to the doctoral examination and thus begin the doctoral studies process. Please note that the application must be received by the Faculty's Office for Doctoral Studies no later than three weeks before the respective faculty council meeting. The receipt stamp is considered the date of submission. You can find the dates of their meetings here.\nFinal Phase \u2013 about one year:\nOnce the last review has been submitted, there is a 14-day period, during which the dissertation and comments can be read the Faculty of Mechanical Engineering's professors, and a two day objection period.\nIn order for us to extend the correct written invitation to the oral examination, we need at least ten days in advance. This means that the oral examination will be held no earlier than 26 days after the last review and comments have been submitted.\nThe one-year deadline for publishing your dissertation begins on the day of your oral examination. It is also possible that you may need to make changes to your dissertation. Any changes to your dissertation topic will be noted in the transcript and also communicated to you again by the Doctoral Office of the Faculty of Mechanical Engineering.\nThe doctoral certificate cannot be issued until the mandatory dissertation copies and a confirmation from the supervisor have been submitted.\nOnce you have received the certificate, you can officially call yourself a \"doctor.\"\nFooter\nRWTH\nRWTH Main Page\nServices\nOpen Positions\nContact and Maps\nLegal Notice\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility Statement\nSitemap\nInstitutions\nDean\u2019s Office\nForschungszentrum J\u00fclich\nStudent Council\n\u00a9 2026 RWTH Aachen University\nSocial Media\nFacebook\nInstagram\nLinkedin", "links": [["Skip to Content", "https://www.maschinenbau.rwth-aachen.de/cms/Maschinenbau/Studium/Nach-dem-Studium/Promotion/Waehrend-der-Promotion/~nahi/Ablauf/?lidx=1#main"], ["Skip to Main Navigation", "https://www.maschinenbau.rwth-aachen.de/cms/Maschinenbau/Studium/Nach-dem-Studium/Promotion/Waehrend-der-Promotion/~nahi/Ablauf/?lidx=1#main-nav-control"], ["Skip to Quick Access", "https://www.maschinenbau.rwth-aachen.de/cms/Maschinenbau/Studium/Nach-dem-Studium/Promotion/Waehrend-der-Promotion/~nahi/Ablauf/?lidx=1#quick-start-control"], ["Skip to Search", "https://www.maschinenbau.rwth-aachen.de/cms/Maschinenbau/Studium/Nach-dem-Studium/Promotion/Waehrend-der-Promotion/~nahi/Ablauf/?lidx=1#searchbar"], ["Skip to Footer", "https://www.maschinenbau.rwth-aachen.de/cms/Maschinenbau/Studium/Nach-dem-Studium/Promotion/Waehrend-der-Promotion/~nahi/Ablauf/?lidx=1#footer"], ["RWTHonline", "https://online.rwth-aachen.de/"], ["RWTHcontacts", "https://rwthcontacts.rwth-aachen.de/"], ["RWTHmoodle", "https://moodle.rwth-aachen.de/"], ["Intranet", "https://intranet.rwth-aachen.de/en"], ["Dining Hall Menus", "https://www.studierendenwerk-aachen.de/en/eating-drinking/me